From 3b4f245a8cd51302b50698d762663f2501e9ef7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:03:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] build(retrieval-server): drop xhtml2pdf, reportlab,
 Markdown and their closure

markdown and xhtml2pdf leave requirements.txt, and constraints.txt loses
every pin that existed only for them: xhtml2pdf, reportlab, svglib, pyHanko,
pyhanko-certvalidator, oscrypto, asn1crypto, Markdown, html5lib,
python-bidi, arabic-reshaper, cssselect2, tinycss2, webencodings, uritools,
tzlocal, lxml and pypdf. Dry-run resolves of requirements.txt with
constraints.txt (Linux, CPython 3.11) before and after, held to the same
versions, differ by exactly these 18 packages and change no other version,
so nothing else depends on them (langchain_text_splitters imports lxml only
optionally, for HTML splitters this service does not use). About 38 MB of
site-packages leave the image.

constraints.txt stays, without pins, because CI and the Dockerfile pass it.
pypdf remains a test-only pin in requirements-dev.txt, and pypdfium2 stays
pinned in requirements.txt. The dependency tests check both files.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01R4WFJ4gcPzabKrzbRdXcQF
